load @term/seed/code/machine/turing
  find turing-machine

# Computational complexity: the study of how much resource (time, space) a computation needs as the input grows, the
# refinement of computability that asks not just whether but how efficiently. The classes P (solvable in polynomial
# time) and NP (verifiable in polynomial time) and the open question of whether they coincide are its center. Where
# computability draws the line of the possible, complexity draws the line of the feasible. The form carries the Turing
# machine whose resource use is measured.
form complexity-class
  link machine, like turing-machine
